{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/llm-framework.md` §\"Comparing the engines\" says each engine record in `rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` output names \"the verdict's `runner` and `model` and the provider-reported `ran_model`\". `_provenance` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`) reads `verdict[\"provider_provenance\"][\"ran_model\"]`, and the value is always `null` when the configured model has no fallback chain.\n\nObserved 2026-11-13 on origin/main `aa1681bb531`. A live Bedrock run (`REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`, a 1-row labels file holding `0128-9a17-79db-450e`) completed both engines (pipeline `model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, agentic `model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, both `runner=pydantic_ai`) with `ran_model: null` on both.\n\n## Root cause\n`PydanticAIRunner.run` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py`) builds `provider_provenance` with `provenance_for(...)`, which has no `ran_model` field. It writes `provider_provenance[\"ran_model\"]` only inside `if fallback_targets:` (after the run, from the answering candidate). A config with no fallback chain, such as `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml`, never gets the key, so every consumer that reads `provider_provenance.ran_model` sees `None`: the engine-comparison harness, and the replay corpus readers (`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:326`, `tier1.py`, `tier2.py`). The plan-review verdict and its sidecar already carry `provider_provenance` intact for both engines. Evidence: a production `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar from this repo's fallback-chain config records `ran_model`. The record is dropped at the runner, not in the gate.\n\n## Approach\nIn `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, after the run, set `provider_provenance[\"ran_model\"] = ran_model` unconditionally. For a fallback chain, keep the existing reassignment from the answering candidate first. For a single model, `ran_model` is the provider-qualified string the runner already computes and passes as the result's `model`. No verdict logic changes. `provider_provenance` is verdict/sidecar metadata and never enters the signed manifest (`src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py` and `plan_review/attest.py` do not read it), so signed material is unchanged. No schema change is needed: `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` allows additional properties, and `provider_provenance` is an unconstrained object in the step-input schemas. No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A `PydanticAIRunner` run with no fallback chain returns `provider_provenance.ran_model` equal to the provider-qualified model it ran (for example `bedrock:us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0`), in both single-turn and agentic modes; proved by a new test in `tests/unit/test_bedrock_vendor_profiles.py` that drives the real Bedrock provider through a scripted client.\n- [ ] Fallback-chain attestation is unchanged: `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py` passes.\n- [ ] Provenance passthrough and harness tests pass: `pytest tests/unit/test_verdict_provenance.py tests/unit/test_verdict_provenance_wiring.py tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py`.\n- [ ] A 1-row live engine comparison with `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml` records a non-null `ran_model` for both engines.\n\n## Testing\nWrite the new runner test first and watch it fail (`ran_model` is `None`), then fix `runner.py`. Run the files above, `make verify`, and the 1-row live comparison."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794591379490908650,"uuid":"3fab457b-9598-4eba-bfd0-7f8ee9ff7969"}